  "_about": "Everything you can carry (D89). One entry per item: id (never change it once used: saves refer to it), name, plural (when it differs), category (food, drink, medical, tool, material, junk), weight in kg, stack (how many make one stack), and what it does: food and drink (points of hunger and thirst, out of 100), heal (health, over a few seconds). Add an item by adding an entry; the loot tables (loot.json) say where it turns up. tags: what an item can stand in for in a recipe (D107: 'clean_water', 'water_container', 'sharp', 'fire', 'fabric', ...); a recipe asking for a tag takes any item that has it. leaves: what's left when it's used up (a bottle of water leaves an empty bottle). D111: firewood comes from trees (an axe) and loot; river water is drinkable but makes you ill unless boiled. D112: a book (category \"book\") teaches the recipes in its \"teaches\" list when read (15 s, in the inventory); what you've learnt is yours for good. D114: a pot of bigos is \"bigos:<what's in it>:<servings>:<reheats>\" (e.g. bigos:KMG:6:2): its name, food and weight come from that and the template's \"evolved\" block (D116: ingredients by letter, base, servings, reheats, food per quality step, quality names, what the empty pot becomes; Game/Items/Evolved.cs). A new dish is a template and its recipes. D115: fresh / stale: days (an hour played each, x the sandbox's food.spoil) it stays fresh, then stale, before it's rotten; no fresh: it doesn't go off (tins, jars, dried things).",
